  "tagline": "The standard spatial extension for PostgreSQL: geometry, geography, rasters and topology in SQL.",
  "description": "PostGIS turns PostgreSQL into a full spatial database. It adds geometry and geography types, hundreds of OGC/ISO SQL/MM functions (ST_Intersects, ST_Buffer, ST_DWithin and so on), GiST and SP-GiST spatial indexing, raster support, topology, 3D and routing via pgRouting, all usable alongside ordinary relational data and transactions. Built on GEOS, PROJ and GDAL, it is the reference open-source GIS backend and is available on nearly every managed Postgres service. The 3.7 release was in release-candidate stage in October 2026, with 3.6.x the current stable line.",
